1. Project Overview
Section Summary

This project focuses on modernizing a legacy retail ETL ecosystem that struggled with fragmented data sources, delayed reporting, and scalability limitations. The solution implements a cloud-native Azure-based lakehouse platform that consolidates retail sales, inventory, customer, vendor, and e-commerce data into a unified analytics environment. Using Azure Data Factory, Azure Databricks, Delta Lake, and Power BI, the platform enables scalable data ingestion, transformation, governance, and enterprise reporting through Medallion Architecture.

1.1 Description
1.1.1 Executive Context

Retail enterprises generate massive amounts of operational and customer data across multiple systems including POS applications, ERP platforms, CRM systems, supplier portals, and e-commerce platforms. In legacy environments, these systems operate independently, causing data silos, inconsistent reporting, and slow business decision-making.

Business teams face challenges such as:

Delayed daily sales reporting
Inventory mismatches across stores
Duplicate customer records
Manual reconciliation using spreadsheets
Poor scalability of on-prem ETL jobs during seasonal sales

Leadership lacks a centralized and trusted analytics platform to monitor sales performance, customer behavior, inventory utilization, and operational KPIs in near real-time.

1.1.2 Technical Solution Narrative

The project modernizes the legacy ETL framework into a scalable Azure Unified Retail Data Platform capable of:

Ingesting structured and semi-structured retail datasets
Supporting batch and incremental data processing
Standardizing and cleansing enterprise retail data
Delivering governed analytical datasets
Providing centralized dashboards for business users

The solution leverages:

Azure Data Factory (ADF) for orchestration and ingestion
Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 (ADLS Gen2) as centralized storage
Azure Databricks + PySpark for scalable transformations
Delta Lake for ACID-compliant data processing
Azure Synapse Analytics / SQL Warehouse for reporting-ready datasets
Power BI for executive and operational dashboards

The platform follows the Medallion Architecture (Bronze → Silver → Gold) model to improve data reliability, maintainability, and analytics performance.

